# Root certificates to trust for TLS: a few that many web servers' chains go back to.
# Any kind of program.
#
#   use crypto.roots;
#   call Roots.TrustAll;            # X509.Trust each of them
#
# Each is the root's DER as Windows' certificate store has it (its SHA-256 fingerprint is
# beside it, to check against the CA's). They're only a few, all RSA: which roots to trust is
# for each project to decide, and it brings any others to X509.Trust, which takes RSA, P-256
# and P-384 keys. A root expires on its date, and new ones come along: this list will want
# updating.

use crypto.x509;

phi.Roots:Library
